2. Definitions.—In these rules, unless the context otherwise requires,—
(1) 'Act' means the Madhya Pradesh Nagarpalikaon ki Adhiniyam, 1956;
(5)(b) 'Authority' means the Bhopal Municipal Corporation for building permission within its limits;
(5)(c) 'Authority' in relation to development permission means the Municipal Corporation or Council concerned, provided that for plots up to 500 sq m the question of whether separate development permission is required is subject to Development Plan conformity;
(20) 'Ground coverage' means the area of land covered by the plinth at ground floor level;
(38) 'High-rise building' means a building having height more than 15.0 metres;
(47) 'Open space' means an area forming an integral part of the plot, left open to the sky.

14. Documents required for development permission.—An application for development permission shall be accompanied by:
(a) site plan showing the boundaries, dimensions and area of the plot;
(b) copy of title deed or agreement to purchase;
(c) location plan;
(d) such other documents as the Authority may specify.

16. Documents required for building permission.—An application for building permission under Rule 9 shall be accompanied by:
(a) building plans prepared by a registered architect;
(b) structural design certificate;
(c) site plan and location plan;
(d) no objection certificates from relevant departments;
(e) proof of payment of application fee under Rule 21.
